.TH "CSSUNITVALUE.VALUE" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnitValue.value \- CSSUnitValue: value property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]value\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R]
interface represents the number of units.
.SH VALUE
A number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code creates a \f[CR]CSSPositionValue\f[R] from individual
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] constructors, then queries the
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue.value\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pos = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSPositionValue(
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(5, \(dqpx\(dq),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(10, \(dqpx\(dq),
);

console.log(pos.x.value); \f[I]// 5\f[R]
console.log(pos.y.value); \f[I]// 10\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue.unit\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
Using the CSS Typed OM
.IP \(bu 2
